\section{Lyapunov Energy Invariance: Dynamical Certainty}
Let $\Theta(t)$ denote the SupraKernel state vector and define the
Lyapunov functional:
\[
V_{\text{kernel}}(\Theta) = \Theta^\top P \Theta,
\]
with $P$ positive definite. Autonomous stability requires:
\[
\frac{dV_{\text{kernel}}}{dt}
\le -\gamma \|\Theta\|^2 + C,
\]
where $\gamma > 0$ is the damping coefficient and $C$ bounds external
perturbations.

\begin{theorem}[Deterministic Autonomous Stability]
If $\gamma > 0$ dominates the perturbation bound $C$, then the SupraKernel
trajectory $\Theta(t)$ remains confined to a compact globally attractive
set $\mathcal{B}$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Using $V_{\text{kernel}} \ge \lambda_{\min}(P)\|\Theta\|^2$, we obtain:
\[
\dot{V}_{\text{kernel}}
\le -\frac{\gamma}{\lambda_{\min}(P)} V_{\text{kernel}} + C.
\]
Applying Grönwall's inequality:
\[
V_{\text{kernel}}(t)
\le V_{\text{kernel}}(0)e^{-\alpha t}
+ \frac{C}{\alpha}(1 - e^{-\alpha t}),
\]
with $\alpha = \gamma/\lambda_{\min}(P)$. Thus,
\[
\|\Theta(t)\|
\le \sqrt{\frac{C}{\alpha \lambda_{\min}(P)}},
\]
establishing global boundedness.
\end{proof}

Lyapunov invariance elevates certainty from probabilistic to deterministic:
failure becomes physically impossible under the governing dynamics.

